  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Addressing supply-side trade and habitat degradation to conserve the Critically endangered Tonkin Snub-nosed Monkey in Quan Ba, Vietnam</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will reduce poaching and illegal habitat destruction of the Tonkin Snub-nosed Monkey (TSNM) by focusing on improving forest management by local authorities and communities. Specific activities include: (1) providing direct protection from hunting and trade of the resident population of the TSNM through a gun confiscation program, an assessment of wildlife traders and trade routes, and support of community-based patrolling in Quan Ba; (2) reducing anthropogenic pressure on the TSNM population and their habitat by identifying hotspots of habitat conversion through remote sensing, mapping the extent of Lysimachia and cardamom cultivation, and developing an action plan for reduced impact Lysimachia and cardamom cultivation.</narrative>
  </description>
